\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218043903}\'a768-105.  Attorneys for Commission.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218043903}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 A
.  The Tax Commission shall employ a Chief Attorney to be designated "General Counsel" and other attorneys each to be designated "attorney" who shall be the legal advisors for the Commission and are authorized to appear for and represent the Commission in
 any and all litigation that may arise in the discharge of its duties.
\par B.  The General Counsel or the district attorney shall initiate criminal actions for violations of the tax laws of this state in the district court of the county in which the defendant r
esides or maintains a place of business.  The attorneys for the Tax Commission may prosecute such criminal actions or may, upon request of a district attorney, appear and assist in the prosecution of such actions initiated by the district attorney.
\par C.  For purposes of this section, the term "tax laws of this state" means any law of the State of Oklahoma which levies, imposes, provides for administration of, or in any way relates to a tax, fee, or revenue raising property which is collected by or req
uired to be deposited with the Commission.
\par D.  The General Counsel and attorneys shall devote all of their time to the Commission and their salaries shall be fixed by the Commission.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Amended by Laws 1983, c. 275, \'a7 3, emerg. eff. June 24, 1983; Laws 1984, c. 292, \'a7
