\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5011857 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218043951}\'a768-219.1.  Abatement of tax liability and interest and penalties accruing thereto - Settlement agreement - Considerations.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
{\*\bkmkend _Toc218043951}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5011857 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5011857 A
.  In accordance with the provisions of the amendment to Section 5 of Article X of the Oklahoma Constitution as set forth in Senate Joint Resolution No. 32 of the 2nd Session of the 48th Oklahoma Legislature, the Oklahoma Tax Commission is hereby authoriz
ed to abate all or any portion of tax liability and interest and penalties accruing thereto, pursuant to a settlement agreement entered into with a taxpayer, if the Tax Commission finds, by clear and convincing evidence, that:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx720\tx2700\tx3600\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5011857 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5011857 1.  Collection of the tax liab
ility and interest and penalties accruing thereto would reasonably result in the taxpayer declaring bankruptcy;
\par 2.  The tax is uncollectible due to insolvency of the taxpayer resulting from factors beyond the control of the taxpayer or for other similar cause beyond the control of the taxpayer;
\par 3.  The tax liability is attributable to actions of a person other than the taxpayer and it would be inequitable to hold the taxpayer liable for the tax liability; or
\par 4.  In cases of nonpayment of trust fund taxes, the taxes were not collected by the taxpayer from its customer and the taxpayer had a good faith belief that collection of the taxes was not required.
\par B.  The Tax Commission may consider the following circumstances, in addition to any other aggravating or mitigating circumstances, in determining whether or not to enter into an agreement pursuant to the provisions of this section:
\par 1.  Whether the taxpayer has made efforts in good faith to comply with the tax laws of this state;
\par 2.  Whether the taxpayer has benefited from nonpayment of the tax; and
\par 3.  Involvement of the taxpayer in economic activity from which the tax liability originated.
\par C.  All agreements entered into pursuant to the provisions of this section shall provide for the collection of all or a portion of the tax liability if at all possible, and in all cases collection of the tax liability shall take precedence over collection
 of interest and penalties.
\par D.  Any abatement of tax liability authorized by this section shall only be granted by a unanim
ous vote of the members of the Tax Commission.  The decision of the members of the Tax Commission in denying the abatement of any tax liability pursuant to this section shall be final and no right of appeal to any court may be taken from such decision.

\par E.  In any case where the amount of tax liability to be abated pursuant to an agreement entered into pursuant to the provisions of this section exceeds Twenty-five Thousand Dollars ($25,000.00), the agreement shall not become effective until it shall have
 been approved by one of the judges of the district court of Oklahoma County, after a full hearing thereon.  Such judge shall be assigned to the matter by the chief judge on a rotating basis.
\par F.  The provisions of this section shall not be construed to grant any legal right to any taxpayer for the abatement of any tax liability.  A decision to grant abatement of tax liability pursuant to the provisions of this section shall be a discretionary 
act within the authority of the members of the Tax Commission.
\par G.  No appointed or elected official shall be eligible to seek relief pursuant to any of the provisions of this section.
\par H.  The Tax Commission shall promulgate rules to implement the provisions of this section.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
