\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218043961}\'a768-227.1.  Illegal or invalid state tax laws - Process for obtaining refund of amounts paid.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218043961}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 A
.  Notwithstanding the provisions of any state tax law relating to or providing for the refund of taxes erroneously paid, no taxpayer shall be entitled to nor be allowed any refund of taxes, penalties or interest paid pursuant to a state tax law subsequen
tly determined by a final decision of a court of competent jurisdiction to be illegal or invalid under the Constitution or laws of this state or of the United States, unless such taxpayer shall have timely availed himself or herself of the remedies and pr
oc
edures provided by Section 207, 221, 226 or 815 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes to protest or challenge such tax, or, where the remedies provided by such sections are unavailable because the tax has not yet been assessed or proposed against such taxp
ayer, such taxpayer shall have brought an action for declaratory judgment in the district court to declare such tax or tax law illegal or invalid.
\par B.  The provisions of this section shall apply to all state taxes, and shall also apply to the refund of any tax imposed by any municipality or county of this state where, under applicable law, such tax is collected by the Oklahoma Tax Commission.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1994, c. 278, \'a7 36, eff. Sept. 1, 1994.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218043962}\'a768-228.  Hearings on claims for refunds.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218043962}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 (
a) If, upon the hearing as required by Section 227 of this title, the Tax Commission finds that such tax was erroneously paid through mistake of fact, or computation or misinterpretation of law, it shall enter its written order allowing said claim for ref
und, which refund may be paid to the taxpayer as provided by law, or credited against any taxes due or to become due by the taxpayer as the case may be; otherwise, the Tax Commission shall deny said claim.  The taxpayer shall have the right of appeal to t
he Supreme Court from a decision of the Commission denying said claim for refund as provided in Section 225 of this article.
\par (b) Any order entered by the Tax Commission, disallowing a claim for refund, shall become final within thirty-
one (31) days from the date it is entered, unless an appeal is prosecuted therefrom, in which event said order shall not become final until the appeal shall have been determined.  In the event the Tax Commission allows said claim for refund, it shall pay 
the claimant the amount of refund, so allowed out of funds in the official depository clearing account of the Tax Commission, derived from collections in said fund from the same source from which the overpayment occurred; and an appropriation of so much o
f 
said fund as is necessary to pay said claims for refund erroneously paid or collected is hereby made; provided, that in the case of refunds due hereunder to taxpayers who are required to remit taxes to the Tax Commission on a monthly or quarterly basis, t
he Commission may, in lieu of a refund of the tax erroneously paid, credit the account of the taxpayer for such amount.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Laws 1965, c. 414, \'a7 2; Laws 1978, c. 211, \'a7 4, emerg. eff. April 19, 1978.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid15081770 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218043963}\'a768-228.1.  Payment of refunds.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkend _Toc218043963}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15081770 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid15081770 E
xcept as otherwise provided by law, claims for refunds which are required to be paid by the Oklahoma Tax Commission shall be paid from funds in the official depository clearing account of the Tax Commission, derived from collections from the same source f
rom which the overpayment occurred.  Provided, in the case of refunds due to taxpayers who are required to remit taxes to the Tax Commission on a monthly or quarterly basis, the Tax Commission may, in lieu of such refund, credit the account of the taxpaye
r for such amount.  If current collections from the same source are insufficient to pay refunds, available cash funds from the unclassified taxes account may be used for such purpose.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15081770 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid15081770 Added by Laws 1999, c. 390, \'a7 4, emerg}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 . eff. June 8, 1999.  Amended by }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid15081770 Laws 2011, c. 348, \'a7 1.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11283 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
