\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 b.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Cigarettes" shall mean 
and include any roll for smoking, made wholly or in part of tobacco, irrespective of size or shape and whether or not such tobacco is flavored, adulterated, or mixed with any other ingredient, the wrapper or cover of which is made of paper}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid7484759 , leaves, string,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436  or any other substance or material, excepting tobacco.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 c.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
Tobacco Products" shall mean any }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid7484759 bidis,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid4462965  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
cigars, cheroots, stogies, smoking tobacco (including granulated, plug cut, crimp cut, ready rubbed, and any other kinds and forms of tobacco suitable for 
smoking in a pipe or cigarette), chewing tobacco (including cavendish, twist, plug, scrap, and any other kinds and forms of tobacco suitable for chewing), however prepared; and shall include any other articles or products made of tobacco or any substitute
 therefor.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 d.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
  "Sale" shall mean any transfer for a consideration, exchange, barter, gift, offer for sale, and distribution in any manner or by any means whatsoever.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 e.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   "Wholesaler" and/or "jobber" is defined to mean a person, firm, or corporation organize
d and existing, or doing business primarily to sell cigarettes to, and render service to retailers in the territory such person, firm or corporation chooses to serve; that purchases cigarettes directly from the manufacturer; that at least seventy-five per
cent (75%) of whose gross sales are made at wholesale; to other than their own retail stores, that handles goods in wholesale quantities and sells through salesmen, advertising, and/or sales promotion devices; that carries at all times at his or its princ
ip
al place of business a representative stock of cigarettes and tobacco products for sale, and that comes into the possession of cigarettes for the purpose of selling them to retailers or to persons outside or within the state who might resell or retail suc
h cigarettes to consumers.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 f.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
  The word "Sub-Jobber" is defined to mean any person in this state who does not purchase cigarettes and tobacco products from a manufacturer and who acquires stamped cigarettes and tobacco products from a wholesaler, at least s
eventy-five percent (75%) of which are for purposes of resale to retailers in this state, or to persons for the purpose of resale only.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 g.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "Retailer}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
" means any person in this state who is engaged in the business of selling cigarettes and tobacco products at retail and any person selling cigarettes through vending machines.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 h.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
  "Manufacturer's representative, or manufacturer's salesman" shall mean any person working for or under the supervision of a manufacturer and whose action is not controlled by the wholesaler or retailer.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 i.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "Consumer}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
" shall mean a person who comes into possession of cigarettes or tobacco products for the purpose of consuming them, giving them away, or disposing of them in a way other than by sale, barter, or exchange.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 j.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "Drop }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
shipment" shall mean and include any delivery of cigarettes or tobacco products received by any person within this state when payment for such cigarettes or tobacco products is made to the shipper or seller by or through a person other than the consignee.

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 k.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "Sell}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
 at retail", "sale at retail", and "retail sales" shall mean and include any transfer of title to cigarettes and tobacco products for a valuable consideration, made in the ordinary course of trade or usual conduct of the seller's business, to the purchase
r for consumption or use.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 l.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "Sell at}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
 wholesale", "sale at wholesale", and "wholesale sales" shall mean and include any transfer of title to cigarettes and tobacco products for a valuable consideration, made in the ordinary course of trade or usual cond
uct of the wholesaler's business, to the retailer for the purpose of resale.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 m.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436   }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10818828 "}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
Basic costs of cigarettes and tobacco products" shall mean the invoice cost of cigarettes and tobacco products to the retailer or wholesaler, as the case may be, or the replacement cost of cigarettes and tobacco products to the retailer or wholesaler, as 
the case may be, within thirty (30) days prior to the date of sale in the quantity last purchased, whichever is lower, less all trade discounts, except the customary discounts
 for cash, to which shall be added the full face value of any stamps which may be required by any cigarette and tobacco products tax act of this state or federal act now in effect or hereafter enacted, if not already included by the manufacturer in }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid7484759 the}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436  list price}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10315012 .}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12018712 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1949, p. 107, \'a7 2, emerg. eff. May 31, 1949.  Renumbered from Title 15, 
\'a7 599.2 by Laws 1981, c. 211, \'a7 7, emerg. eff. June 1, 1981.  Amended by Laws 1993, c. 366, \'a7 29, eff. Sept. 1, 1993; }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \dbch\af11\insrsid11747436\charrsid12350832 \hich\af2\dbch\af11\loch\f2 \hich\f2 
Laws 2002, c. 76, \'a7\loch\f2  2, emerg. eff. April 15, 2002.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \dbch\af11\insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1451930 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044065}\'a768-328.  Sales at less than cost; penalty.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044065}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1451930 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a
.  It shall be unlawful for any retailer or wholesaler, with intent to injure competitors or destroy or substantially lessen competition, to advertise, offer to sell, or sell, at retail or wholesale, cigarettes and tobacco products at less than cost to su
ch retailer or wholesaler, as the case may be.  Any retailer or wholesaler who violates the provisions of this section shall be guilty of a misdemeanor and be punishable by fine of not more than Five Hundred Dollars ($500.00).
\par b.  Evidence of advertisement,
 offering to sell, or sale of cigarettes and tobacco products by any retailer or wholesaler at less than cost to him as defined in this act shall be prima facie evidence of intent to injure competitors and to destroy or substantially lessen competition.

\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1451930 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1949, p. 108, \'a7 3, emerg. eff. May 31, 1949.  Renumbered from Title 15, }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 \'a7}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436  599.3 by Laws 1981, c. 211, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 \'a7}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
 7, emerg. eff. June 1, 1981.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12478270 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044066}\'a768-329.  Cost to wholesaler; meaning.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044066}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12478270 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a
.  The term "cost to the wholesaler" shall mean the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" to the wholesaler plus the "cost of doing business by the wholesaler", as evidenced by the recognized statistical and cost accounting practices in allocati
on of overhead costs and expenses, paid or incurred, and must include, without limitation, labor costs (including salaries or drawing accounts of owners, salaries of executives and officers, or general and special allocations and charges made by parent or
ganizations), rent, depreciation, selling costs, maintenance of equipment, delivery costs, all types of licenses, taxes, insurances, and advertising, and any other cost.
\par b.  In the absence of proof of a lesser cost of doing business by the wholesaler making the sale, the "cost of doing business by the wholesaler" shall be presumed to be two per centum (2%) of the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" to the whol
esaler, plus cartage to the retail trade, if performed or paid for by the wholesaler, whi
ch cartage cost, in the absence of proof of a lesser cost, shall be deemed to be three-fourths of one per centum (3/4 of 1%) of the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" to the wholesaler.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12478270 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1949, p. 108, \'a7 4, emerg. eff. May 31, 1949.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid7170870   Renumbered from Title 15, \'a7 599.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 4}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid7170870  by Laws 1981, c. 211, \'a7 7, emerg. eff. June 1, 1981.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2642977 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044067}\'a768-330.  Cost to the retailer; meaning.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044067}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2642977 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a
.  The term "cost to the retailer" shall mean the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" to the retailer plus the "cost of doing business by the retailer", as evidenced by the recognized statistical and cost accounting practices in allocation of 
overhead costs and expenses, paid or incurred, and must include, without limitation, labor (including salaries or drawing accounts of owners, salaries of executives and officers, or general and special allocations and charges made by parent organizations)
, 
rent, depreciation, selling costs, maintenance of equipment, delivery costs, all types of licenses, taxes, insurance, and advertising, and any other cost:  Provided, that any retailer who, in connection with the retailer's purchase, receives not only the 
discounts ordinarily allowed upon purchases by a retailer but also, in whole or in part, discounts ordinarily allowed upon purchases by a wholesaler, shall, in determining "cost to the retailer", pursuant to this subsection, add the "cost of doing busines
s by the wholesaler", as defined in Section 4 of this act, to the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" to said retailer, as well as the "cost of doing business by the retailer".
\par b.  In the absence of proof of a lesser cost of doing business by the retailer making the sale, the "cost of doing business by the retailer" shall be presumed to be six per centum (6%) of the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" to the retailer
, plus cartage to the retail outlet if performed or paid for by the re
tailer (and not previously included in the charge by the wholesaler), which cartage cost, in the absence of proof of a lesser cost, shall be deemed to be three-fourths of one per centum (3/4 of 1%) of the basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products to t
he retailer.
\par c.  In the absence of proof of a lesser cost of doing business, the "cost of doing business by the retailer", who, in connection with the retailer's purchase, receives not only the discounts ordinarily allowed upon purchases by a retailer but a
lso, in whole or in part, the discounts ordinarily allowed upon purchases by a wholesaler, shall be presumed to be six percentum (6%) of the sum of the "basic cost of cigarettes and tobacco products" and the "cost of doing business by the wholesaler".

\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2642977 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1949, p. 109, \'a7 5, emerg. eff. May 31, 1949.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
