\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10168702 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 As used in the Motor Fuel Tax Code:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 1.  "Act" or "this act" means the Motor Fuel Tax Code;}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
2.  "Agricultural purposes" means clearing, terracing or otherwise preparing the ground on a farm; preparing soil for planting and fertilizing, cultivating, raising and harvesting crops; raising and feeding livestock and poultry; building fences; pumping 
water for any and all uses on the farm, including irrigation; building roads upon any farm by the owner or person farming same; operating milking machines; sawing wood
 for use on a farm; producing electricity for use on a farm; movement of tractors, farm implements and equipment from one field to another and use of farm tractors to move farm products from farm to market;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
3.  "Biodiesel" means a fuel comprised of mono-alkyl esters of long chain fatty acids generally derived from vegetable oils or animal fats, commonly known as "B100", that is commonly and commercially known or sold as a fuel that is suitable for use in a h
ighway vehicle.  The fuel meets this requirement if, without further processing or blending, the fuel is a fluid and has practical and commercial fitness for use in the propulsion of a highway vehicle;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
4.  "Biodiesel blend" means a blend of biodiesel fuel with petroleum-based diesel fuel, commonly designated as "Bxx", where "xx" represents the volume percentage of biodiesel fuel in the blend, and that is commonly and commercially known or sold as a fuel
 that is suitable for use in a highway vehicle.  The fuel meets this requirement if, without further processing or blending, the fuel is a fluid and has practical and commercial fitness for use in the propulsion of a highway vehicle;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
5.  "Blend stock" means any petroleum product component of gasoline, such as naphtha, reformate, or toluene, that can be blended for use in a motor fuel without further processing.  However, the term does not include any substance that:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 a.\tab 
will be ultimately used for consumer nonmotor-fuel use, and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 b.\tab is sold or removed in drum quantities (55 gallons) or less at the time of the removal or sale;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
6.  "Blended fuel" means a mixture composed of gasoline or diesel fuel and another liquid, other than a de minimis amount of a product such as carburetor detergent or oxidation inhibitor, that can be used as a fuel in a highway vehicle.  This term include
s gasohol, ethanol and fuel grade ethanol;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 7.  "Blender" means any person that produces blended motor fuel outside the bulk transfer/terminal system;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 8.  "Blending" means the mixing of one or more petroleum products, with or without another p
roduct, regardless of the original character of the product blended, if the product obtained by the blending is capable of use or otherwise sold for use in the generation of power for the propulsion of a motor vehicle, an airplane, or a motorboat.  The te
rm does not include that blending that occurs in the process of refining by the original refiner of crude petroleum or the blending or products known as lubricating oil and greases;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 9.  "Bulk end user" means a person who receives into the person's own storage facilities in transport truck lots of motor fuel for the person's own consumption;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 10.  "Bulk plant" means a motor fuel storage and distribution facility that is not a terminal and from which motor fuel may be removed at a rack;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 11.  "Bulk transfer" means any transfer of motor fuel from one location to another by pipeline tender or marine delivery within the bulk transfer/terminal system;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 12.  "Bulk transfer/terminal system" means the motor fuel distribution system consisting of refineries, pipelines, ve
ssels, and terminals.  Gasoline in a refinery, pipeline, vessel, or terminal is in the bulk transfer/terminal system.  Motor fuel in the fuel supply tank of any engine, or in any tank car, rail car, trailer, truck, or other equipment suitable for ground t
ransportation is not in the bulk transfer/terminal system;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 13.  "Tax Commission" or "Commission" means the Oklahoma Tax Commission;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 14.  "Compressed natural gas" means a volume of natural gas consisting primarily of methane which has been reduced to approxi
mately one percent (1%) of its original volume for purposes of storage and for use as a fuel in motor vehicles;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 15.  "Consumer" means the user of the motor fuel on the public highways of this state;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
16.  "Dead storage" means the amount of motor fuel that will not be pumped out of a storage tank because the motor fuel is below the mouth of the draw pipe.  For purposes of Section 500.1 et seq. of this title, a dealer may assume that the amount of motor
 fuel in dead storage is two hundred (200) gallons for a tank with a capacity of less than ten thousand (10,000) gallons and four hundred (400) gallons for a tank with a capacity of ten thousand (10,000) gallons or more;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 17.  "Delivery" means the placing of motor fuel or any liquid into the fuel tank of a motor vehicle;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
18.  "Destination state" means the state, territory, or foreign country to which motor fuel is directed for delivery into a storage facility, a receptacle, a container, or a type of transportation equipment for the purpose of resale or use;}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 19.  "D
iesel fuel" means any liquid, including but not limited to, biodiesel, biodiesel blend or other diesel blended fuel, that is commonly or commercially known or sold as a fuel that is suitable for use in a diesel-powered highway vehicle.  A liquid meets thi
s requirement if, without further processing or blending, the liquid has practical and commercial fitness for use in the propulsion engine of a diesel-powered highway vehicle.  Except as provided in subsection B of Section 500.4 of this title, "diesel fue
l" does not include jet fuel sold to a buyer who is registered with and certified by the Internal Revenue Service to purchase jet fuel subject to the Internal Revenue Service;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 20.  "Diesel-powered highway vehicle" means a motor vehicle operated on a highway that is propelled by a diesel-powered engine;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 21.  "Distributor" means a person who acquires motor fuel from a supplier or from another distributor for subsequent sale or use;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 22.  "Dyed diesel fuel" means diesel fuel that is required to be dyed pursuant t
o United States Environmental Protection Agency rules or is dyed pursuant to Internal Revenue Service rules or pursuant to any other requirements subsequently set by the United States Environmental Protection Agency or Internal Revenue Service including a
ny invisible marker requirements;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 23.  "Eligible purchaser" means a person who has been authorized by the Commission pursuant to Section 500.23 of this title to make the election pursuant to Section 500.22 of this title;}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 24.  "Enterer" includes any person w
ho is the importer of record, pursuant to federal customs law, with respect to motor fuel.  If the importer of record is acting as an agent, the person for whom the agent is acting is the enterer.  If there is no importer of record of motor fuel entered i
nto this state, the owner of the motor fuel at the time it is brought into this state is the enterer;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 25.  "Entry" means the importing of motor fuel into this state.  Motor fuel brought into this state in the fuel tank of a motor vehicle shall not be deemed
 to be an "entry" if not removed from the fuel tank except as used for the propulsion of that motor vehicle, except to the extent that motor fuel was acquired tax free for export or a refund of tax was claimed as a result of exportation from the state fro
m which that motor fuel was transported into this state;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
26.  "Export" means to obtain motor fuel in this state for sale or other distribution in another state.  In applying this definition, motor fuel delivered out of state by or for the seller constitutes
 an export by the seller and motor fuel delivered out of state by or for the purchaser constitutes an export by the purchaser;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 27.  "Exporter" means any person, other than a supplier, who purchases motor fuel in this state for the purpose of transporting or delivering the fuel to another state or country;}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
28.  "Farm tractor" means all tractor-type, motorized farm implements and equipment but shall not include motor vehicles of the truck-type, pickup truck-type, automobiles, and other motor vehicles required
 to be registered and licensed each year pursuant to the provisions of the motor vehicle license and registration laws of this state;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 29.  "Fuel transportation vehicle" means any vehicle designed for highway use which is also designed or used to transport motor fuels and includes transport trucks and tank wagons;}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
30.  "Gasoline" means all products, including but not limited to, gasoline blend stocks, commonly or commercially known or sold as gasoline that are suitable for use as a motor fuel.  Gasoline does
 not include products that have an American Society for Testing Materials ("A.S.T.M.") octane number of less than seventy-five (75) as determined by the "motor method".  Except as provided in subsection B of Section 500.4 of this title, "gasoline" does no
t include aviation gasoline provided that the buyer is registered to purchase aviation gasoline free of tax and the seller obtains certification of such fact satisfactory to the Commission prior to making the sale;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 31.  "Gasoline blend stocks" includes any 
petroleum product component of gasoline, such as naphtha, reformate, or toluene, that can be blended for use in a motor fuel.  The term shall not include any substance that will be ultimately used for consumer nonmotor-fuel use and is sold or removed in d
rum quantities of 55 gallons or less at the time of the removal or sale;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 32.  "Gross gallons" means the total measured motor fuel, exclusive of any temperature or pressure adjustments, in U.S. gallons;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 33.  "Heating oil" means a motor fuel that is burned in a boiler, furnace, or stove for heating or industrial processing purposes;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 34.  "Highway vehicle" means a self-propelled vehicle that is designed for use on a highway;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
35.  "Import" means to bring motor fuel into this state by any means of conveyance other than in the fuel supply tank of a motor vehicle.  In applying this definition, motor fuel delivered into this state from out of state by or for the seller constitutes
 an import by the seller, and motor fuel delivered into this state from out of state by or for the purchaser constitutes an import by the purchaser;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
36.  "Import verification number" means the number assigned by the Commission with respect to a single transport truck delivery into this state from another state upon request for an assigned number by an importer or the transporter carrying motor fuel in
to this state for the account of an importer;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 37.  "In this state" means the area within the border of this state, including all land within the borders of this state owned by the United States of America;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 38.  "Indian country" means:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 a.\tab 
land held in trust by the United States of America for the benefit of a federally recognized Indian tribe or nation,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 b.\tab 
all land within the limits of any Indian reservation under the jurisdiction of the United States Government, notwithstanding the issuance of any patent, and including rights-of-way running through the reservation,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 c.\tab all dependent Indian communities within the borders of the United States whether within the original or subsequently acquired territo
ry thereof, and whether within or without the limits of a state, and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 d.\tab 
all Indian allotments, the Indian titles to which have not been extinguished, including individual allotments held in trust by the United States or allotments owned in fee by individual Indians subject to federal law restrictions regarding disposition 
of said allotments and including rights-of-way running through the same.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
The term shall also include the definition of Indian country as found in 18 U.S.C., Section 1151;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 39.  "Indian trib
e", "tribes", or "federally recognized Indian tribe or nation" means an Indian tribal entity which is recognized by the United States Bureau of Indian Affairs as having a special relationship with the United States.  The term shall also include the defini
tion of a tribe as defined in 25 U.S.C., Section 479a;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 40.  "Invoiced gallons" means the gallons actually billed on an invoice in payment to a supplier;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 41.  "K-1 kerosene" means a petroleum product having an A.P.I. gravity of not less than forty degrees (40\'b0), at a temperature of sixty degrees (60\'b0
) Fahrenheit and a minimum flash point of one hundred degrees (100\'b0) Fahrenheit with a sulphur content not exceeding five one-hundredths percent (0.05%) by weight;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
42.  "Liquefied natural gas" means a volume of natural gas consisting primarily of methane which has been cooled to approximately negative two hundred sixty (-260) degrees Fahrenheit in order to convert it to a liquid state for purposes of storage and use
 as a fuel in motor vehicles;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 43.  "Liquid" means any substance that is liquid in excess of sixty degrees (60\'b0) Fahrenheit and a pressure of fourteen and seven-tenths (14.7) pounds per square inch absolute;}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 44.  "Motor fuel" means gasoline, diesel fuel and blended fuel;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 45.  "Motor fuel transporter" means a person who transports motor fuel outside the bulk terminal/transfer system by transport truck or railroad tank car;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 46.  "Motor vehicle" means every automobile, truck, truck-tractor or any motor bus or self-propelled vehicle not operated or driven upon fixed rails or tracks.  The term does not include:}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 a.\tab 
farm tractors or machinery including tractors and machinery designed for off-road use but capable of movement on roads at low speeds,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 b.\tab a vehicle operated on rails, or}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 c.\tab machinery designed principally for off-road use;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10168702 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
47.  "Net gallons" means the motor fuel, measured in U.S. gallons, when corrected to a temperature of sixty degrees (60\'b0) Fahrenheit (13\'b0 Celsius) and a pressure of fourteen and seven-tenths (14.7) pounds per square inch (psi);}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 48.  "Permissive supplier" means an out-of-state supplier that elects, but is not required, to have a supplier's license pursuant to Section 500.1 et seq. of this title;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
49.  "Person" means natural persons, individuals, partnerships, firms, associations, corporations, estates, trustees, business trusts, syndicates, this state, any county, city, municipality, school district or other political subdivision of the state, fed
erally recognized Indian tribe, or any corporation or combination acting as a unit or any receiver appointed by any state or federal court;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 
50.  "Position holder" means the person who holds the inventory position in motor fuel in a terminal, as reflected on the records of the terminal operator.  A person holds the inventory position in motor fuel when that person has a contract with the termi
nal operator for the use of storage facilities and terminaling services for fuel at the terminal.  The term includes a terminal operator who owns fuel in the terminal;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid5326925 51.  "Public highway" means every road, toll 
