\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044173}\'a768-500.10-1.  Ethanol credit \endash  Refund claims process.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044173}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15546388 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 A.  As used in this section:
\par 1.  \'93Ethanol\'94 means a blend of gasoline and ethyl alcohol consisting of not more than fifteen percent (15%) ethyl alcohol by volume; and
\par 2.  \'93Retail dealer\'94 means the type of dealer described by paragraph 53 of Section 500.3 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes.
\par B.  Unless the federal government mandates the use of reformulated fuel in an area within the State of Oklahoma in nonattainment with the National Ambient Air Quality Standards, there shall be allowed as a credit against 
the tax levy imposed pursuant to paragraph 1 of subsection A of Section 500.4 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes in the amount of one and six-tenths cents ($0.016) for each gallon of ethyl alcohol which is contained in ethanol sold by a retail dealer.

\par C.  Notwithstanding any other provision of the Oklahoma Motor Fuel Tax Code to the contrary, the retail dealer described by subsection A of this section may make the claim for refund from the Oklahoma Tax Commission.  The refund claim process for the cred
it authorized by this section shall be substantially the same as the refund claims process authorized by the Motor Fuel Tax Code for other refunds provided by law.
\par D.  Each claim for refund filed pursuant to this section shall be accompanied by such documentation as may be required by the Tax Commission that the retail dealer reduced the retail price for each gallon of ethyl alcohol which is contained in ethanol sol
d, and for which the credit authorized by this section is claimed, by one and six-tenths cents ($0.016) and that such cost savings was economically provided to the purchaser of the ethanol fuel.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15546388 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2005, c. 294, \'a7 2, eff. Jan. 1, 2006.
