\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid8810751 Definitions.
\par As used in the Oklahoma Sales Tax Code:
\par 1.  \'93Alcoholic beverages\'94 means beverages that are suitable for human consumption and contain one-half of one percent (0.5%) or more of alcohol by volume;
\par 2.  \'93Bottled water\'94 means water that is placed in a safety sealed container or package for human consumption.  Bottled water is calorie-free and does not contain sweeteners or other additives except that it may contain:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid8810751 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid8810751 a.\tab antimicrobial agents,
\par b.\tab fluoride,
\par c.\tab carbonation,
\par d.\tab vitamins, minerals, and electrolytes,
\par e.\tab oxygen,
\par f.\tab preservatives, and
\par g.\tab only those flavors, extracts, or essences derived from a spice or fruit;
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid8810751 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid8810751 3.  \'93Bundled transaction\'94
 means the retail sale of two or more products, except real property and services to real property, where the products are otherwise distinct and identifiable, and the products are sold for one nonitemized price.  A bundled transa
ction does not include the sale of any products in which the sales price varies, or is negotiable, based on the selection by the purchaser of the products included in the transaction.  As used in this paragraph:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid8810751 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid8810751 a.\tab \'93distinct and identifiable products\'94
