le to the customer in paper or electronic form including, but not limited to, an invoice, bill of sale, receipt, contract, service agreement, lease agreement, periodic notice of rates and services, rate card, or price list.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li2016\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid8810751 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid8810751 
A transaction that otherwise meets the definition of a bundled transaction shall not be considered a bundled transaction if it is:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2736\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2736\itap0\pararsid8810751 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid8810751 (1)\tab 
the retail sale of tangible personal property and a service where the tangible personal property is essential to the use of the service, and is provided exclusively in connection with the service, and the true object of the transaction is the service,

\par (2)\tab 
the retail sale of services where one service is provided that is essential to the use or receipt of a second service and the first service is provided exclusively in connection with the second service and the true object of the transaction is the sec
ond service,
\par (3)\tab a transaction that includes taxable products and nontaxable products and the purchase price or sales price of the taxable products is de minimis.  For purposes of this subdivision, \'93de minimis\'94 means the seller\rquote 
s purchase price or sales price of taxable products is ten percent (10%) or less of the total purchase price or sales price of the bundled products.  Sellers shall use either the purcha
se price or the sales price of the products to determine if the taxable products are de minimis.  Sellers may not use a combination of the purchase price and sales price of the products to determine if the taxable products are de minimis.  Sellers shall u
