\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid3215097 Requirements for entering into Streamlined Sales and Use Tax Agreement}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 .{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044457}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2240721 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 The Oklahoma Tax Commission shall not enter into the Streamlined Sales and Use Tax Agreement unless the Agreement requires each state to abide by the following requirements:
\par 1.  Simplified State Rate.  The Agreement must set restrictions to limit over time the number of state rates;
\par 2.  Uniform Standards.  The Agreement must establish uniform standards for the following:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid2240721 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a.\tab the sourcing of transactions to taxing jurisdictions,
\par b.\tab the administration of exempt sales, and
\par c.\tab sales and use tax returns and remittances;
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2240721 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
3.  Central Registration.  The Agreement must provide a central, electronic registration system that allows a seller to register to collect and remit sales and use taxes for all signatory states;
\par 4.  No Nexus Attribution.  The Agreement must provide that registration with the central registration system and the collection of sales and use taxes in the signatory states will not be used as a factor in determining whether the seller has nexus with a 
state for any tax;
\par 5.  Local Sales and Use Taxes.  The Agreement must provide for reduction of the burdens of complying with local sales and use taxes through the following:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid2240721 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a.\tab restricting variances between the state and local tax bases,
\par b.\tab 
requiring states to administer any sales and use taxes levied by local jurisdictions within the state so that sellers collecting and remitting these taxes will not have to register or file returns with, remit funds to, or be subject to independent audi
ts from local taxing jurisdictions,
\par c.\tab restricting the frequency of changes in the local sales and use tax rates and setting effective dates for the application of local jurisdictional boundary changes to local sales and use taxes, and
\par d.\tab providing notice of changes in local sales and use tax rates and of changes in the boundaries of local taxing jurisdictions;
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2240721 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
6.  Monetary Allowances.  The Agreement must outline any monetary allowances that are to be provided by the states to sellers or certified service providers.  The Agreement must allow for a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14943711 
review}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436  of the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14943711 costs and benefit
s of administration and collection of sales and use taxes incurred by states and sellers under the existing sales and use tax laws at the time of adoption of the Agreement and the proposed Streamlined Sales and Use Tax Agreement}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 ;
\par 7.  State Compliance.  The Agreement must require each state to certify compliance with the terms of the Agreement prior to joining and to maintain compliance, under the laws of the member state, with all provisions of the Agreement while a member;
\par 8.  Consumer Privacy.  The Agreement must require each state to adopt a uniform policy for certified service providers that protects the privacy of consumers and maintains the confidentiality of tax information; and
\par 9.  Advisory Councils.  The Agreement must provide for the appointment of an advisory council of private sector representatives and an advisory council of nonmember state representatives to consult with in the administration of the Agreement.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2240721 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2001, c. 272, \'a7 7, eff. Nov. 1, 2001.  Amended by}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid13452740  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Laws 2003, c. 413, \'a7 8, eff. Nov. 1, 2003.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044458}\'a768-1354.21.  Simplified Sales and Use Tax Administration Act - Effect of Agreement.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044458}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 T
he Agreement authorized by this act is an accord among individual cooperating sovereigns in furtherance of their governmental functions.  The Agreement provides a mechanism among the member states to establish and maintain a cooperative, simplified system
 for the application and administration of sales and use taxes under the duly adopted law of each member state.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2001, c. 272, \'a7 8, eff. Nov. 1, 2001.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044459}\'a768-1354.22.  Simplified Sales and Use Tax Administration Act - Persons benefitted by Agreement.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044459}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 A
.  The Agreement authorized by this act binds and inures only to the benefit of this state and the other member states.  No person, other than a member state, is an intended beneficiary of the Agreement.  Any benefit to a person other than a state is esta
blished by the law of this state and the other member states and not by the terms of the Agreement.
\par B.  Consistent with subsection A of this section, no person shall have any cause of action or defense under the Agreement or by virtue of this state\rquote s approv
al of the Agreement.  No person may challenge, in any action brought under any provision of law, any action or inaction by any department, agency, or other instrumentality of this state, or any political subdivision of this state on the ground that the ac
tion or inaction is inconsistent with the Agreement.
\par C.  No law of this state, or the application thereof, may be declared invalid as to any person or circumstance on the ground that the provision or application is inconsistent with the Agreement.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2001, c. 272, \'a7 9, eff. Nov. 1, 2001.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044460}\'a768-1354.23.  Simplified Sales and Use Tax Administration Act - Certified service provider defined - Seller liability.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044460}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436 A.  A certified service provider is the agent of a seller, with whom the certified service provider has contracted, for the collection and remittance of sales and use taxes.  As the seller\rquote 
s agent, the certified service provider is liable for sales and use tax due each member state on all sales transactions it processes for the seller except as set out in this section.
\par A seller that contracts with a certified service provider is not liable to the state for sales or use tax due on transactions processed by th
e certified service provider unless the seller misrepresented the type of items it sells or committed fraud.  In the absence of probable cause to believe that the seller has committed fraud or made a material misrepresentation, the seller is not subject t
o audit on the transactions processed by the certified service provider.  A seller is subject to audit for transactions not processed by the certified service provider.  The member states acting jointly may perform a system check of the seller and review 
the seller\rquote s procedures to determine if the certified service provider\rquote s system is functioning properly and the extent to which the seller\rquote s transactions are being processed by the certified service provider.
\par B.  A person that provides a certified automated system is responsible for the proper functioning of that system and is liable to the state for underpayments of tax attributable to errors in the functioning of the certified automated system.  A seller tha
t uses a certified automated system remains responsible and is liable to the state for reporting and remitting tax.
\par C.  A seller that has a proprietary system for determining the amount of tax due on transactions and has signed an agreement establishing a performance standard for that system is liable for the failure of the system to meet the performance standard.

\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2001, c. 272, \'a7 10, eff. Nov. 1, 2001.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044461}\'a768-1354.24.  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid3215097 Amnesty for uncollected or unpaid sales or use taxes}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 .
{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044461}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10951836 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 A.  If the Oklahoma Tax Commission enters into the Streamlined Sales and Use Tax Agreement under Section 1354.18 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes and s}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid11747436 
ubject to the limitations in this section:
\par 1.  Amnesty shall be granted for uncollected or unpaid sales or use taxes to a seller who registers to pay or to collect and remit applicable sales or use taxes on sales made to purchasers in this state in accordance with the terms of the Streamlined Sale
s and Use Tax Agreement, provided that the seller was not registered in this state in the twelve-month period preceding the effective date of this state's participation in the Agreement; and
\par 2.  The amnesty will preclude assessment for uncollected or unpaid sales or use tax together with penalty or interest for sales made during the period the seller was not registered in this state, provided registration occurs within twelve (12) months of t
he effective date of this state\rquote s participation in the Agreement.
\par B.  The amnesty is not available to a seller with respect to
 any matter or matters for which the seller received notice of the commencement of an audit and which audit is not yet finally resolved including any related administrative and judicial processes.
\par C.  The amnesty is not available for sales or use taxes already paid or remitted to the state or to taxes collected by the seller.
\par D.  The amnesty is fully effective, absent the seller\rquote s fraud or intentional misrepresentation of a material fact, as long as the seller continues registration and continues payment or
 collection and remittance of applicable sales or use taxes for a period of at least thirty-six (36) months.  The statute of limitations applicable to asserting a tax liability during this thirty-six-month period shall be tolled.
\par E.  The amnesty is applicable only to sales or use taxes due from a seller in its capacity as a seller and not to sales or use taxes due from a seller in its capacity as a buyer.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2003, c. 413, \'a7 17, eff. Nov. 1, 2003.
