s electronic funds transfer and electronic data interchange programs may file according to the following schedule:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14617700 1.  For sales from the first day through the fifteenth day of each month, the tax shall be due
 and payable on the twentieth day of such month and remitted to the Tax Commission by electronic funds transfer.  A taxpayer will be considered to have complied with the reporting requirements of this paragraph if, on or before the twentieth day of such m
onth, the taxpayer paid at least ninety percent (90%) of the liability for that fifteen-day period or at least fifty percent (50%) of the taxpayer\rquote 
s liability in the immediate preceding calendar year for the same month as the month in which the fifteen-day period occurs; and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
