\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044607}\'a768-1635.  Purpose - Definitions.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044607}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\tx2736\tx3456\tx4176\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9591001 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 A.  The purpose of this act is to enact a licensing program for outdoor display fireworks}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid11747436  for Oklahoma entities}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567  and a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 licensing}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 
 program for individuals conducting outdoor fireworks displays in this state.  The purpose of these programs is to ensure a level of competence that promotes safety for the public, fire service personnel, and fireworks display operators and their employee
s and service personnel.  It is not the purpose of this act to regulate United States Department of Transportation Division }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 1.4G}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567  co
nsumer fireworks as defined by NFPA standards or paragraph 2 of Section 1622 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 B.  As used in this act:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 1.  \'93Licensed outdoor display operator\'94
 means an individual who by experience, training, and examination recognized and approved by the State Fire Marshal has demonstrated the necessary knowledge and ability to safely assemble, discharge and supervise out
door display fireworks in accordance with NFPA 1123;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 2.  "Operator" shall have the same meaning as "licensed outdoor display operator", as defined in paragraph 1 of this subsection;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 3.  \'93Display fireworks\'94
 means fireworks devices that are primarily intended for commercial displays which are designed to produce visible and/or audible effects by combustion, deflagration or detonation.  Display fireworks include, but are not limited to,
 salutes containing more than two grains (130mg) of explosive composition, aerial shells containing more than forty (40) grams of pyrotechnic compositions and other exhibition display items th
at exceed the limits for consumer fireworks according to the United States Department of Transportation (DOT);}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 4.  \'93Event\'94
 means any function or gathering at which there will be a fireworks display.  If a function or gathering lasts more than one (1) day, each day is a separate event.  Event does not include any function or gathering at which only consumer firewor
ks, as defined in paragraph 2 of Section 1622 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes, will be used exclusively;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 5.  "Distributor" means any person e
ngaged in the business of making sales of display fireworks as defined in paragraph 3 of Section 1622 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes or materials to Oklahoma-licensed or -permitted entities for the}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
 purpose of providing fireworks or}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567  pyrotechnic display services in this state.  A distributor may sell display fireworks only to Oklahoma}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
-licensed or -permitted entities}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  An out-of-state distributor shall not be required to obtain an Oklahoma license when selling exclusively to a holder of an Oklahoma manuf
acturer, distributor, or wholesaler license;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 6.  \'93NFPA\'94 means the National Fire Protection Association;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par 7}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93NFPA 1123\'94 means the NFPA publication entitled \'93NFPA 1123: Code for Fireworks Display\'94
, 2010 Edition or any subsequent edition that has been adopted by the State Fire Marshal by rule;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par 8}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93NFPA 1124\'94 means the NFPA publication entitled \'93NFPA 1124: Code for Manufacture, Transportation, Storage, and Retail Sale of Fireworks and Pyrotechnic Articles\'94
, 2006 Edition or any subsequent edition that has been adopted by the State Fire Marshal by rule;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par 9}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93NFPA 1126\'94 means the NFPA publication entitled \'93NFPA 1126: Standards for the Use of Pyrotechnics Before a Proximate Audience\'94
, 2011 Edition or any subsequent edition that has been adopted by the State Fire Marshal by rule;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par 10}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93Outdoor fireworks display\'94 means a presentation of display fireworks for a public or private gathering as defined by NFPA 1123;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 

\par 11}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93Proximate pyrotechnics\'94 means pyrotechnic devices for professional use only, used outdoors or indoor
s, that are similar to consumer fireworks in chemical composition but that are not intended for consumer use, and that are defined by NFPA 1126 as 1.4G or 1.4S fireworks or pyrotechnics;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par 12}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93Proximate pyrotechnic display\'94
 means the use of pyrotechnic devices and materials, 1.4G or 1.4S fireworks or pyrotechnics when any portion of the audience is closer than permitted by NFPA 1123, and subject to NFPA 1126 requirements; and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 

\par 13}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid657567 .  \'93Sponsor\'94 means any person or organization which contracts with a licensed entity, licensed distributor or licensed outdoor display operator to conduct a fireworks display.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9591001 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2011, c. 238, \'a7 1, eff. May 1, 2012.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13843031 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044608}\'a768-1636.  Fireworks display - Licenses or permits.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218044608}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13843031 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid13988886 A.  An individual or entity shall have the appropriate Oklahoma license or permit to conduct an outdoor fireworks display on or after January 1, 2013.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\tx2736\tx3456\tx4176\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13843031 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid13988886 
B.  To receive a manufacturer, distributor or wholesaler license, an applicant shall make application to the State Fire Marshal on a form prescribed by the State Fire Marshal.  The application shall be accompanied by the required fee.  An individual seeki
ng a license as a sole proprietor or on behalf of a business entity shall be at least twenty-one (21) years
 of age and shall not have been convicted of or pled guilty or nolo contendere to any state or federal felony.  In the case of a business seeking a license, no officer or member of its governing board shall have been convicted of or pled guilty or nolo co
ntendere to any state or federal felony.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid13988886 
Nothing in this act shall be construed as applying to shipping, sale, possession or use of display fireworks when displayed by holders of a permit for a public display to be conducted in accordance with the rules and
 regulations of the State Fire Marshal Commission.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid13988886 
Applications for permits for display fireworks shall be submitted in writing prior to the date of display to the Authority Having Jurisdiction (AHJ) as defined by the NFPA 1123 where the display is to occur.  If the display is in an area outside the juris
diction of a municipality, application for the permit shall be submitted in writing to the Office of the State Fire Marshal ten (10) days prior to the date of the display.  Every display shall be under the 
direction of a competent, responsible, licensed outdoor display operator, of legal age, and shall be conducted under the code of regulations as adopted by the State Fire Marshal Commission.  The individual or organization applying for a permit shall submi
t to the AHJ evidence of a general liability insurance policy in an amount of not less than One Million Dollars ($1,000,000.00) or the amount set forth by the local governing authority.  Before a permit is granted, a local fire inspector or an agent of th
e State Fire Marshal shall inspect and approve or reject the site of the display.  No permit so granted shall be transferable.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13843031 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 2011, c. 238, \'a7 2, eff. May 1, 2012.  Amended by Laws 2012, c. 369, \'a7
 3, emerg. eff. June 8, 2012.
