\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 The gross production tax provided for by this act is hereby levied and collected for the following specific purposes, to wit:
\par First:  The tax on the land shall be collected and distributed by the county treasurer to the same funds as other land taxes in the taxing district shall go and be distributed.
\par Second:  The tax on the buildings, mill, machinery, appliances, equipments and property used in the production of textile manufactured products shall go to and be distributed by the county treasurer to the various funds as follows:
\par One thirtieth (1/30) of the said tax to the State of Oklahoma for the general revenue purposes.
\par Fifteen thirtieths (15/30) of the said tax to the school district in which the mill is located for school purposes.
\par Seven thirtieths (7/30) of the said tax to the city or township in which the said mill is located for city or township purposes, as the case may be.
\par Two thirtieths (2/30) of the said tax to the sinking funds of the county school district and city or township in which the said mill is located to be divided in proportion to the respective levies made for that year for the said sinking funds.
\par Five thirtieths (5/30) of the said tax to the county general fund.
\par Said apportionment and distribution for the said funds shall be made by the county treasurer of the said county.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Laws 1927, c. 111, p. 175, \'a7 4; Laws 1955, p. 391, \'a7 3; Laws 1965, c. 215, \'a7 1.

