eater than twenty (20) miles per hour but not greater than twenty-five (25) miles per hour and is manufactured in compliance with the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration standards for low-speed vehicles in 49 C.F.R. 571.500;
\par 4.  The term \'93automobile\'94 means and includes every motor vehicle constructed and used solely for the transportation of persons for purposes other than for hire or compensation;
\par 5.  The term \'93motorcycle\'94 means and includes every motor vehicle designed to travel on not more than three wheels other than an all-terrain vehicle;
\par 6.  The term \'93truck\'94 means and includes every motor vehicle constructed or used for the transportation of property not falling within the definition of truck-tractor, trailer or semitrailer, as herein defined;
\par 7.  The term \'93truck-tractor\'94 means and includes every motor vehicle of the truck type designed to draw or support the front end of a semitrailer;
\par 8.  The term \'93trailer\'94 means and includes any vehicle designed to be drawn by a truck, tractor or a truck-tractor, but supported upon its own wheels;
\par 9.  The term \'93semitrailer\'94 means and includes any vehicle designed to be attached to, and having its front end supported by a truck, tractor, or truck-tractor;
\par 10.  The term \'93motor bus\'94 means and includes every motor vehicle constructed so as to carry persons, and which is used or rented to carry persons for compensation;
\par 11.  The term \'93manufactured home\'94
