\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10444639 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218044693}\'a768-2357.1A-1.  Task Force for the Study of State Tax Credits and Economic Incentives.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkend _Toc218044693}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14313805 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10444639 A.  There is hereby created the Task Force for the Study of State Tax Credits and Economic Incentives.
\par B.  The Task Force shall consist of ten (10) members to be appointed or selected as follows:
\par 1.  The Chair of the Appropriations and Budget Committee of the Oklahoma House of Representatives;
\par 2.  The Chair of the Appropriations Committee of the Oklahoma State Senate;
\par 3.  The Chair of the Revenue and Taxation Subcommittee of the Appropriations and Budget Committee of the Oklahoma House of Representatives;
\par 4.  The Chair of the Senate Finance Committee;
\par 5.  The Director of the Office of Management and Enterprise Services or a designee;
\par 6.  The State Treasurer or a designee;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10444639 7.  The Oklahoma Secretary of State or a designee;
\par 8.  Minority Leader of the Oklahoma House of Representatives;
\par 9.  Minority Leader of the Oklahoma State Senate; and
\par 10.  The State Auditor and Inspector.
\par C.  The Task Force shall conduct an organizational meeting not later than September 30, 2011.  A majority of the members present at the organizational meeting or any subsequent meeting shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of any action taken includin
g the preparation and approval of the final report required by subsection I of this section.
\par D.  The cochairs of the Task Force shall be the member who is the Chair of the Revenue and Taxation Subcommittee of the Appropriations and Budget Committee and the member who is the Chair of the Finance Committee of the State Senate.
\par E.  The Task Force shall be authorized to meet as necessary in order to perform the duties imposed upon it.  Legislative members of the Task Force shall be reimbursed for travel expenses pursuant to the provisions of Section 456 of Title
 74 of the Oklahoma Statutes.  Other members of the Task Force shall be reimbursed as provided by the appointing authority.
\par F.  The Task Force shall conduct a study regarding all state tax credits regardless of the tax type against which such credit may be claimed and any other economic incentives that affect state or local tax liabilities.  The study shall include, but shall 
not be limited to:
\par 1.  The j{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname PersonName}}us{\*\xmlclose}tification for the enactment of any state tax credits based upon the relevant economics of the applicable ind{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname PersonName}}us{\*\xmlclose}
try or economic sector affected;
\par 2.  The economic impact related to the utilization of state tax credits;
\par 3.  Analysis of the utilization of the credits by tax credit purchasers;}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid10444639 4.  The impact of tax credits on any and all economic sectors of the state economy;
\par 5.  The adequacy or inadequacy of state tax credits or other economic incentives; and
\par 6.  Such other matters related to state tax credits or economic incentives as the Task Force deems relevant.
\par G.  The Task Force shall be subject to the provisions of:
\par 1.  The Oklahoma Open Meeting Act; and
\par 2.  The Oklahoma Open Records Act.
\par H.  Staff assistance for the Task Force shall be provided by the staff of the Oklahoma Ho{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname PersonName}}us{\*\xmlclose}e of Representatives and the State Senate.
\par I.  The Task Force shall produce a final written report of its findings and any recommendations regarding transferable tax credits.  The report shall be submitted to the Governor, the Speaker of the Oklahoma Ho{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname PersonName}}
us{\*\xmlclose}e of Representatives and the President Pro Tempore of the State Senate not later than December 31, 2011.
\par J.  The provisions of this section shall cease to have the force and effect of law and the Task Force shall terminate effective January 1, 2012.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
