\par 1.  "Federally regulated investment company" means a qualified small business capital company as defined by Section 2357.61 of this title and that is licensed by the United States Small Business Administration or the United States Department of Agricultur
e and which qualifies as one of the following types of entities:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0\pararsid2840673 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid16064819 a.\tab a Small Business Investment Company, or
\par b.\tab a Specialized Small Business Investment Company, or
\par c.\tab a Rural Business Investment Company, or
\par d.\tab a Community Development Entity as defined by Section 45D of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended; and
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2840673 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid16064819 
2.  "Qualified small business capital company" means an entity meeting the requirements of Section 2357.61 of this title.
\par B.  Federally regulated investment companies shall be exempt from the reporting requirements of subsections C and G of Section 2357.64 of this title.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid16064819 
C.  As a condition of the exemption authorized by this section, the federally regulated investment company shall provide to the Oklahoma Tax Commission not later than March 15 each year:
\par 1.  A copy of the federal license issued by the applicable federal regulatory entity;
\par 2.  A copy of all reports and compliance documents required by the federal regulators; and
\par 3.  A copy of the annual financial audit of the federally regulated investment company.
\par D.  A federally regulated investment company shall also prepare an annual summary report that discloses:
\par 1.  All investments made in for-profit business entities during the preceding calendar year;
\par 2.  The primary business address of each for-profit business entity in which any investment was made;
\par 3.  A statement of the business activity of each of the for-profit business entities described in paragraphs 1 and 2 of this subsection;
\par 4.  The type of investment instrument used to make the investment; and
\par 5.  A status report of all investments made by the federally regulated investment company.
\par E.  The federally regulated investment company shall transmit a copy of the annual summary prescribed by subsection D of this section to the committees or subcommittees of the Oklahoma House of Representatives and the Oklahoma State Senate having primary 
jurisdiction over the Small Business Capital Formation Incentive Act, the State Treasurer, the State Auditor and Inspector, the Director of the Office of Management and Enterprise Services and the Oklahoma Tax Commission.
\par F.  The 
report required by subsection D of this section shall be prepared and submitted until all of the monies available to the federally regulated investment fund have been fully invested, all of the investments have been completed and the proceeds from the inv
estment have been disbursed to the equity investors.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
