ss
 during the fiscal year, and it shall be the duty of the State Board of Equalization to ascertain the number of cars required to make the total mileage of cars of such corporation within the period of one (1) year.  Said Board shall ascertain and fix a va
luation upon each particular class of said cars, and the number so ascertained to be required to make the total mileage of the cars of each such corporation, within the period of one (1) year, shall be assessed to the respective corporations, and such ass
es
sment shall be included in the record of the proceedings of the Board and shall be certified by the State Auditor and Inspector to the county clerks of the several counties of the state wherein such cars are operated in the same manner as property of the 
