.  The application for a limit on the fair cash value of homestead property as provided for in Section 8C of Article X of the Oklahoma Constitution shall be made on or before March 15 or within thirty (30) days from and after receipt by the taxpayer of a 
notice of valuation increase, whichever is later.  The application shall be made upon a form prescribed by the Oklahoma Tax Commission, which shall require the taxpayer to certify as to the amount of gross household income.  As used in Section 8C of Artic
le X of the Oklahoma Constitution, \'93gross household income\'94
 shall be as defined in Section 2890 of this title.  Upon request of the county assessor, the Oklahoma Tax Commission shall assist in verifying the correctness of the amount of the gross income.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\tx2736\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid399569 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14617700 
B.  For persons who have previously qualified for the limitation on the fair cash value of homestead property as provided for in Section 8C of Article X of the Oklahoma Constitution, no annual application shall be required in order to be subject to the li
mitation.  However:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14617700 1.  Any such person whose gross household income in any calendar year exceeds }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14097060 
the amount provided for in Section 8C of Article X of the Oklahoma Constitution}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14617700 
shall notify the county assessor and the limitation shall not be allowed for the applicable year; and}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436\charrsid14617700 
2.  Any such person who makes improvements to the property shall notify the county assessor and the improvements shall be assessed in accordance with law by the county assessor and added to the assessed value of the property as provided 
in Section 8C of Article X of the Oklahoma Constitution.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
