\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218045358}\'a768-3502.  Findings and intent of Legislature.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218045358}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 A
.  It is the finding of the Legislature that there exists in this state a continuing need for programs to assist political subdivisions in attracting federal facility development and consequent job creation and ancillary economic growth within this state.
  In order to achieve these essential public purposes, it is necessary to assist and encourage political subdivisions to develop facilities for use by the federal government.
\par B.  It is the intent of the Legislature that:
\par 1.  The State of Oklahoma provide appropriate incentives to assist political subdivisions of this state in attracting qualified federal facilities that hold the promise of significant development of the economy of the State of Oklahoma;
\par 2.  The amount of such incentives provided in connection with a particular federal facility:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a.\tab 
be directly related to the jobs created as a result of the facility locating in the State of Oklahoma, and
\par b.\tab not exceed the estimated net direct state benefits that will accrue to the state as a result of the facility locating in the State of Oklahoma;
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
3.  The Oklahoma Department of Commerce and the Oklahoma Tax Commission implement the provisions of this act and exercise all powers as authorized in this act.  The exercise of powers conferred by this act shall be deemed and held to be the performance of
 essential public purposes; and
\par 4.  Nothing herein shall be construed to constitute a guarantee or assumption by the State of Oklahoma of any debt of a political subdivision nor to authorize the credit of the State of Oklahoma to be given, pledged or loaned to any political subdivision.

\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1993, c. 1, \'a7 2, emerg. eff. Feb. 8, 1993.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218045359}\'a768-3503.  Definitions.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218045359}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 As used in this act:
\par 1.  "Qualified federal facility" means a facility developed after March 1, 1993, by or at the expense of a political subdivision of this state and leased or conveyed to the government of the United States which primarily houses federal employees; provided
, the annual gross payroll for new direct jobs of a qualified federal facility must be projected by the Department of Commerce as having the potential to equal or exceed Fifty Million Dollars ($50,000,000.00) when the facility is fully operational;
\par 2.  "New direct job" means full-time-equivalent employment in a qualified federal facility which did not exist in this state prior to the date of approval by the Department of Commerce of the application of the political subdivision for the qualified fede
ral facility pursuant to the provisions of Section 4 of this act;
\par 3.  "Estimated direct state benefits" means the tax revenues projected by the Department of Commerce to accrue to the state as a result of new direct jobs;
\par 4.  "Estimated direct state costs" means the costs projected by the Department of Commerce to accrue to the state as a result of new direct jobs.  Such costs shall include but not be limited to:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-720\li2016\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\tx1296\tx2016\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin2016\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 a.\tab the costs of education of new state resident children,

\par b.\tab the costs of public health, public safety and transportation services to be provided to new state residents,
\par c.\tab the costs of other state services to be provided to new state residents,
\par d.\tab the costs of employee training and other state services, and
\par e.\tab the costs of physical infrastructure needed to support the facility;
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 
5.  "Estimated net direct state benefits" means the estimated direct state benefits less the estimated direct state costs;
\par 6.  "Net benefit rate" means the estimated net direct state benefits computed as a percentage of gross payroll; provided, the net benefit rate shall not exceed the lesser of five and one-fourth percent (5.25%) or the minimum rate deemed by the Department 
of Commerce to be necessary to result in an incentive payment at a level which will enable the political subdivision to attract the qualified federal facility;
\par 7.  "Political subdivision" means a municipality, a county or a public trust, the beneficiary or beneficiaries of which are a municipality, a county or the State of Oklahoma or a combination thereof;
\par 8.  "Gross payroll" means wages for new direct jobs as defined in paragraph (e) of Section 2385.1 of Title 68 of the Oklahoma Statutes;
\par 9.  "Project term" means the length of time a political subdivision may receive incentive payments pursuant to the provisions of this act; provided, the project term shall not exceed twenty (20) years from the date of the first incentive payment;
\par 10.  "Total net benefit" means the net benefit rate multiplied by the gross payroll over the project term as estimated by the Department of Commerce pursuant to the provisions of subsection C of Section 4 of this act; and
\par 11.  "Develop" means acquire, maintain, construct, improve, enlarge, renew, renovate, replace, lease, equip, furnish or operate.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1993, c. 1, \'a7 3, emerg. eff. Feb. 8, 1993.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218045360}\'a768-3504.  Incentive payments - Amount - Application - Qualifications - Approval - Notice - Additional information.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218045360}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 A
.  A political subdivision may receive quarterly incentive payments from the Oklahoma Tax Commission pursuant to the provisions of this act in an amount which shall be equal to the net benefit rate multiplied by the actual gross payroll of new direct jobs
 for a calendar quarter; provided, the total amount of such payments shall not exceed the total net benefit.
\par B.  In order to receive incentive payments pursuant to the provisions of this act, a political subdivision shall apply to the Oklahoma Department of
 Commerce.  The application shall be on a form prescribed by the Department and shall contain such information as may be required by the Department.
\par C.  The Department shall determine if the applicant is qualified to receive incentive payments pursuant to the provisions of this act and if so, conduct a cost/benefit analysis to determine the estimated net direct state benefits and the net benefit rate 
and to estimate the amount of gross payroll for the project term.  In conducting such cost/benefit analysis,
 the Department shall consider quantitative factors, such as the anticipated level of new tax revenues to the state along with the added cost to the state of providing services, qualitative factors, and such other criteria as deemed appropriate by the Dep
artment.
\par D.  Upon approval of such an application, the Department shall notify the Oklahoma Tax Commission and shall provide the Commission with a copy of the application and the results of the cost/benefit analysis.  The Tax Commission may require the poli
tical subdivision or the qualified federal facility to submit such additional information as may be necessary to administer the provisions of this act.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1993, c. 1, \'a7 4, emerg. eff. Feb. 8, 1993.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid925797 \rtlch\fcs1 \af2\afs40\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af2 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc218045361}\'a768-3505.  Incentive payments - Funding source.{\*\bkmkend _Toc218045361}
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \fi576\li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx576\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f2\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 I
n order to ensure the availability of funds for incentive payments authorized pursuant to the provisions of this act, the Oklahoma Tax Commission shall transfer such amounts as determined by multiplying the net benefit rate provided by the Department of C
ommerce by the gross payroll as determined pursuant to the provisions of subsection A of Section 6 of this act.  Such funds shall be transferred from current withholding tax collections into an agency special account designated for this purpose by the Okl
ahoma Tax Commission at such times as may be deemed necessary by the Tax Commission.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sl240\slmult0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid11747436 Added by Laws 1993, c. 1, \'a7 5, emerg. eff. Feb. 8, 1993.
